  "job": "Moves the enemy where his team wants them: pulled into the pool, pushed off the carry.",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "lore": "Before the light stopped, Dunsom drove his village's flocks home every dusk. The dusk never ended, so the flocks never went in, and he grew very good at moving things that did not want to be moved. He walks with a lantern hung from the hook of a crook taller than he is, and he speaks to enemies the way he once spoke to goats: kindly, firmly and without any doubt about where they will end up. He believes every quarrel can be settled if everyone simply stands in the right place.",
